  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe post-merge batch gate on main `3e47b898b` failed on\n`adaptive_entry_pieces::a_narrow_second_piece_names_its_ramp_stand_in_at_each_level`.\n\n**Cause:** #2383 (for #2232) added `machining2d::pocket::non_sliver_center`.\nIt sent every multi-piece cutter-center area (two or more outer loops)\nthrough a `Region::from_slices` rebuild, even when the sliver scan dropped\nnothing. Clipper's normalisation restarts each loop at another vertex, so a\nmulti-piece pocket's pass starts moved. The narrow second piece's 1x1\ncenter square started at (56, 6) instead of (56, 5), and the test's named\nsite no longer matched. The entry was still a named ramp (no gouge, no\nunnamed plunge), but the move was an unintended side effect and not part of\n#2232's decision.\n\n**Fix:** `non_sliver_center` returns the plain `region.offset(-erode)`\nunchanged unless at least one sliver is actually removed. Regions without\nslivers now come out exactly as they did before #2383, and #2232's sliver\ndrop still applies where a sliver exists. Not a revert: #2383's stock-reach\nclearing and sliver filter stay. The reasoning is in\n`docs/decisions/2426-adaptive-entry-red.md`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before the fix, on `3e47b898b`, the test fails with: `no named ramp stand-in for the pass start (56.000, 5.000) at Z -4.000 ... notes: [\"entry: the pass start (56.000, 6.000) at Z -4.000 ... ramp along the pass instead\", ...]`\n- After the fix, all 5 tests of `adaptive_entry_pieces` pass.\n- New pin `machining2d::pocket::non_sliver_tests::a_multi_piece_center_without_slivers_is_the_plain_offset` (motion lib) fails when the fix is disabled and passes with it.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head `e10ba5ba3`: 20 steps, 0 failed (motion lib incl. adaptive_troch tests that share `non_sliver_center`; motion adaptive_hsm, climb_direction, corner_arc_radius, corner_blend, entry_arc, optimal_load, predrilled_entry, refusal_ghost, rest_zigzag, rest2d, shape_masks, solid_law, top_z_level, xy_arc_entry; app pick_agnostic, pocket_overhead, solid_law_goldens).\n- `adaptive_entry_pieces` (motion): 5/5 pass, including the failing test.\n- `shoulder_adaptive` (app, #2383's own suite, pins the sliver drop and the outside-stock clearing): 9/9 pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe release heavy lanes and the batch tier. The next post-merge run is the confirmation that #2426 asks for.\n\nChangelog: Multi-piece pockets keep their pass starts again; the sliver filter from #2383 no longer reorders pocket areas that have no sliver (#2426)\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2426\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
